From 5c37c9de68da463f2cc9a1a9c27516ced8b629a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:23:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SECURITY-RESCAN-3: read a request body only after
 authentication

The server buffered every POST body, up to 12 MB, before the middleware
that decides who is asking had run, so anonymous connections each
declaring 12 MB could hold a small box's memory without being anybody.
The body is now read after the middleware; a declared Content-Length
over the cap is refused before any of it is held; and the public sign-in
doors read at most 64 KB.

